# The Author reviews every change to the enforcement layer, the governance documents, and the corpus
# (CLAUDE.md; constitution, Security & Agent Governance). Takes effect at publication (ADR 0013), and only
# if branch protection requires code-owner review.
/.claude/    @hareet
/CLAUDE.md   @hareet
/REVIEW.md   @hareet
/.specify/   @hareet
/.github/    @hareet
/corpus/     @hareet

# Spec 000's human-only paths (FR-001; ADR 0017): the gate code only the Author runs, the secret rules, the FR-039
# boundary, agent tool configuration, and the price table.
/tools/gates/            @hareet
/evals/agent-config/     @hareet
/.gitleaks.toml          @hareet
/deploy/agents-engine/   @hareet
/.mcp.json               @hareet
/config/prices*          @hareet

# The other human-only paths spec 000 names (plan §15; ADR 0017; protected-paths.sh): the budgets, the alerts, and the
# kill switch, which the stacks read; the env files; the makefiles make would read before the Makefile, at the root;
# and gitleaks' ignore list, wherever one sits.
/config/budgets*         @hareet
/config/alert*           @hareet
/config/kill-switch*     @hareet
/config/twin-readiness*  @hareet
/deploy/env/             @hareet
/GNUmakefile             @hareet
/makefile                @hareet
**/.gitleaksignore       @hareet
